From d50f14a5435b939e17bd2f15e3127b0c0cc64b59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:16:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] refactor(pathkernel): say what the order does with a
 whole full-width curve and the first row

Review notes of PR #4234. A curve with a Span::Whole full-width mark is
taken after the other ready curves and starts as a plain curve (no
stretch end); the starts match names each case. A row on the first step
(no tool position) is never reversed, on purpose: it runs as the
canonical guide set gives it. The walk builds the planned cuts once and
removes each cut that it takes, in place of a new list at each step.

Refs #4177

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
